      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Woodrow United Methodist Church, built in 1842, is one of Staten Island’s oldest active congregations and was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1982.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodrow_staten_island",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1771, Francis Asbury preached his first sermon in the area at Peter Van Pelt’s home, marking the birth of Methodism on Staten Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/woodrow_staten_island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sandy Ground, founded in 1828 by free African Americans, served as an Underground Railroad stop and was known for its strawberry farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
